I fixed #1203 in commit 7c65218f: /side and /architect now use the same max_tokens the main agent uses with thinking off, on every provider. Build, cargo test (0 failures), clippy with -D warnings and the fmt check all pass.

What was wrong: neither agent set max_tokens at all. A user's cap was ignored by both on every provider, and on Bedrock no maxTokens was sent. I wrote the test first and it failed on HEAD before the fix.

| provider / model | user max_tokens | main | /side before → after | /architect before → after |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| anthropic / claude-sonnet-4-6 | 2048 | 2048 | None → 2048 | None → 2048 |
| anthropic / claude-sonnet-4-6 | unset | None | None → None | None → None |
| bedrock / anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6 | unset | 64000 | None → 64000 | None → 64000 |
| openai / gpt-4o | 1234 | 1234 | None → 1234 | None → 1234 |

The fix: one small helper, AgentConfig::thinking_off_max_tokens(model), called from both agents. On Bedrock it reuses the existing providers::bedrock_max_tokens(model, user, false); on other providers it returns the user's cap. The architect looks up its own model, not the main one. The test (agent_limits_tests::side_and_architect_agents_resolve_max_tokens_like_the_main_agent) takes the expected 64000 from yoagent's preset rather than a typed number, and checks that the preset exists so that row can't pass as None == None.

Thinking: it stays off for both agents, since they answer in one turn. So there is one case where they still differ from the main agent, on purpose: Bedrock with thinking on, where the main agent follows yoagent's thinking-on rule.

How far this is checked: I checked the value on the built agent, not in an actual request. /side and /architect can't be run from -p, so I didn't use the recording stub in tests/bedrock_max_tokens_request.rs. The commit body says this.

Also changed:
• docs/src/configuration/models.md said these agents send no cap; I corrected that sentence.
• I raised the size limit for agent_builder.rs in tests/module_size.rs from 5012 to 5026 lines, with a dated reason.
• I posted the before-table on #1203 before changing any code, and the after-table once the fix was committed.
